From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pylibfdt: build with SWIG 4.3 and newer

do_compile fails against swig 4.4.1:

    scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt_wrap.c:7004:19: error: too few arguments to
    function 'SWIG_Python_AppendOutput'; expected 3, have 2

SWIG 4.3.0 gave SWIG_Python_AppendOutput() a third "is_void" parameter. Code
that SWIG generates itself was updated to match, but libfdt.i carries
hand-written typemaps that call the function directly, and those still pass
two arguments.

Wrap the call so the interface file works with either signature. All three
sites append to a result that is already a value (a property's name, a node
depth, a reserve-map entry), never to a void return, so is_void is 0.

The wrapper is defined after "#include <libfdt.h>" in the %{ %} header block,
which SWIG emits well after its own "#define SWIG_VERSION", so the version test
resolves.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [u-boot 2024.01 is pinned here for RK3566;
fixed upstream in later releases via dtc]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
@@ -18,6 +18,17 @@
 #include "libfdt.h"
 
 /*
+ * SWIG 4.3.0 gave SWIG_Python_AppendOutput() a third "is_void" argument. The
+ * typemaps below are hand-written and so have to pick the right signature
+ * themselves; every one of them appends to a non-void result, so pass 0.
+ */
+#if SWIG_VERSION >= 0x040300
+#define fdt_append_output(result, obj) SWIG_Python_AppendOutput(result, obj, 0)
+#else
+#define fdt_append_output(result, obj) SWIG_Python_AppendOutput(result, obj)
+#endif
+
+/*
  * We rename this function here to avoid problems with swig, since we also have
  * a struct called fdt_property. That struct causes swig to create a class in
  * libfdt.py called fdt_property(), which confuses things.
@@ -1037,7 +1048,7 @@
 			fdt_string(fdt1, fdt32_to_cpu($1->nameoff)));
 		buff = PyByteArray_FromStringAndSize(
 			(const char *)($1 + 1), fdt32_to_cpu($1->len));
-		resultobj = SWIG_Python_AppendOutput(resultobj, buff);
+		resultobj = fdt_append_output(resultobj, buff);
 	}
 }
 
@@ -1076,7 +1087,7 @@
 
 %typemap(argout) int *depth {
         PyObject *val = Py_BuildValue("i", *arg$argnum);
-        resultobj = SWIG_Python_AppendOutput(resultobj, val);
+        resultobj = fdt_append_output(resultobj, val);
 }
 
 %apply int *depth { int *depth };
@@ -1092,7 +1103,7 @@
            if (PyTuple_GET_SIZE(resultobj) == 0)
               resultobj = val;
            else
-              resultobj = SWIG_Python_AppendOutput(resultobj, val);
+              resultobj = fdt_append_output(resultobj, val);
         }
 }
 
